{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775378696-Qnj5hGoCsjYlLEpTsTOm","role":"assistant","created":1775378705,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, there's an issue. Table 2 has 138 values, and 138/6 = 23. So row 23 would be index 23*6 = 138, but that's beyond the array. Let me check - the last row is index 22 (row 23, 0-indexed).\n\nActually wait, the data shows 138 values and 23 rows. Row 23 would be index 22 (0-indexed), so row 23*6:(22+1)*6 = 138:144, but there are only 138 values (indices 0-137).\n\nLet me recalculate. If there are 23 rows and 6 columns each, that's 138 cells. Indices 0-137.\nRow 0: indices 0-5\nRow 1: indices 6-11\n...\nRow 22: indices 132-137\n\nSo row 22 (the 23rd row) would be at indices 132-137.\n\nLet me check that.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_23f066c25834416f9d98dee1","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1980_05_page_41.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Extract table data\ntd_values = re.findall(r'<td>([^<]+)</td>', content)\n\n# Separate tables\ntable1_values = td_values[:230]\ntable2_values = td_values[230:]\n\n# Check table 2 - last row (row 23 - index 22)\nprint(\"Table 2, last row (Mar. 1980):\")\nlast_row_start = (23-1) * 6  # row 23 (0-indexed: 22)\nlast_row = table2_values[last_row_start:last_row_start+6]\nfor i, cell in enumerate(last_row):\n    print(f\"  Col {i}: {cell}\")\n\n# Verify data cells correctly - exclude row headers (col 0 of each row)\n# And exclude any non-numeric values like '*'\n\n# For table 1: columns 1-9 are data (col 6 is '*')\n# For table 2: columns 1-5 are data (all numeric)\n\n# Let me recount from scratch\n\n# Table 1 - all data columns except row header\ntable1_data = []\nfor row_idx in range(23):\n    start = row_idx * 10\n    row = table1_values[start:start+10]\n    # columns 1-9 are data (skip col 0 = row header, col 6 = '*')\n    for col_idx in [1,2,3,4,5,7,8,9]:\n        table1_data.append(row[col_idx])\n\n# Table 2 - all data columns except row header  \ntable2_data = []\nfor row_idx in range(23):\n    start = row_idx * 6\n    row = table2_values[start:start+6]\n    # columns 1-5 are data (skip col 0 = row header)\n    for col_idx in [1,2,3,4,5]:\n        table2_data.append(row[col_idx])\n\n# Filter numeric values\nnumeric_table1 = [v for v in table1_data if v and v[0].isdigit()]\nnumeric_table2 = [v for v in table2_data if v and v[0].isdigit()]\n\nprint(f\"\\nTable 1 numeric data cells: {len(numeric_table1)}\")\nprint(f\"Table 2 numeric data cells: {len(numeric_table2)}\")\nprint(f\"Total: {len(numeric_table1) + len(numeric_table2)}\")\n\n# Clean values (remove commas, footnote markers)\ndef clean_value(v):\n    v = re.sub(r'\\s+[0-9]+/$', '', v)  # footnote like \"7/\"\n    v = re.sub(r'r$', '', v)   # trailing 'r' for revised\n    return v.replace(',', '')\n\ncleaned_table1 = [clean_value(v) for v in numeric_table1]\ncleaned_table2 = [clean_value(v) for v in numeric_table2]\n\n# Count leading 1\ncount1_table1 = sum(1 for v in cleaned_table1 if v and v[0] == '1')\ncount1_table2 = sum(1 for v in cleaned_table2 if v and v[0] == '1')\n\nprint(f\"\\nTable 1 leading 1s: {count1_table1}\")\nprint(f\"Table 2 leading 1s: {count1_table2}\")\nprint(f\"Total: {count1_table1 + count1_table2}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
